"""Deli Counter 0.258.0 (the factory's roadmap 296): the scout view -- a building drawn with only what a body finds its
way by, and carried in its package.

The walker, of 0.257.0's drawing: "we need to find a way to be simple and not noisy visually", and players should see
something "simpler but carry all of the signals needed". `render_axonometric(scout=True)` keeps every wall, opening,
tread, ladder and hole, one line for each flight and hole between storeys, and leaves out furniture, rooms, markers
and dashed lines; `package_drawings` writes it as `drawings/scout.svg`, kept, and names it in `drawings.json`.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `portable_building.py`, `axonometric.py` and `test_package_drawings.py` (anchored hunks); the new
`test_scout_view.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone
(`patches/dc_scout_view/gen_dc_scout_view.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run
refused (`patches/dc_scout_view/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_scout_view.py
    cd deli_counter && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
